{number: 144}
{title: Singing I Go}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
The [C] trusting heart to Jesus clings,
Nor any [F] ill can [C] fear;
Safe sheltered 'neath His loving wings,
And feeling [G7] He is [C] near.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Singing I go along life's road,
Praising the [F] Lord, praising the [C] Lord;
Singing I go along life's road,
For [G7] Jesus has lifted my [C] load.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
The [C] passing cloud may bring its shade,
The [F] tempest blow a-[C] pace;
My trusting soul is not afraid,
Upheld by [G7] His dear [C] grace.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
He [C] gives me peace, He gives me song,
His [F] joy is full and [C] free;
My steps are glad the whole day long,
Since [G7] Jesus walks with [C] me.
{end_of_verse}
